.TH DOMINT 1 2026-11-04 "domint 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
domint \- domain intelligence for threat-intelligence analysts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B domint
.RI [ options ]
.I domain
.RI [ domain ...]
.br
.B domint
.RI [ options ]
.B \-f
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B domint
collects registration, hosting, DNS, certificate, subdomain, reputation and
lookalike data about one or more domains, correlates it, and writes a report
that ranks findings by severity.
Every value in the report can be traced to the query that produced it.
.PP
.B domint
is passive by default: it queries third-party sources only (registries, DNS
resolvers, Certificate Transparency logs and threat-intelligence feeds), so the
investigated domain does not receive traffic from the local address unless
.B \-\-active
is given.
.PP
Domains can be given as host names, URLs or defanged indicators such as
.BR hxxps://example[.]com .
.SH AUTHORIZED USE
Use
.B domint
only against domains that you own or are authorized to assess.
Every investigation carried out for a client requires prior authorization,
formalized in a contract that defines the domains in scope, the techniques
permitted (passive only, or active as well), the period of the assessment and
how the collected data is handled.
This applies to passive mode too; active mode additionally sends requests to
the client's systems.
.SH MODULES
Without module options every module runs except
.BR \-l .
With one or more module options only those run, and their detailed sections
are shown without
.BR \-\-full .
Short module options can be combined:
.B \-wds
is the same as
.BR "\-w \-d \-s" .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-addresses
Addresses, reverse DNS and announcing network (ASN).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dns
DNS records: NS, MX, SPF, DMARC, CAA, DNSSEC, SOA and TXT.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-whois
Registration data (RDAP, falling back to WHOIS).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tls
TLS certificate on port 443.
Contacts the target.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-http
HTTP response on port 80.
Contacts the target.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subdomains
Subdomains from passive sources and their CNAME targets; with
.BR \-\-active ,
which of them answer over HTTP or HTTPS.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reputation
AlienVault OTX, and abuse.ch URLhaus and ThreatFox when
.B ABUSECH_AUTH_KEY
is set.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lookalikes
Typosquatting: which variants of the name are registered and which can receive
mail.
Sends about a thousand DNS queries per domain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIpath\fR"
Read domains from a file, one per line.
Lines starting with
.B #
and blank lines are ignored.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Write the report to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Write the report as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-stix
Write the report as a STIX 2.1 bundle.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-full
Show every section with all collected data.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
In addition to
.BR \-\-full ,
list every query made and append the raw WHOIS, RDAP and HTTP responses.
.TP
.B \-\-active
Contact the targets from the local address: HTTP and TLS requests to the domain
and HTTP/HTTPS probes to its subdomains.
Requires the client's prior written authorization for active testing.
.TP
.B \-\-passive
Never contact the targets, even when
.B \-t
or
.B \-H
is given.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-active .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-subdomains
Skip subdomain enumeration.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-probe
In active mode, skip the HTTP/HTTPS probes of subdomains.
.TP
.BI \-\-resolver " ipv4"
Send DNS queries to this resolver instead of the system ones.
The resolver learns which domains are investigated.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ABUSECH_AUTH_KEY
Key for the abuse.ch APIs; enables URLhaus and ThreatFox lookups.
.TP
.B OTX_API_KEY
Key for AlienVault OTX; raises the rate limit of anonymous requests.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was written.
Failures of individual sources are reported in the Gaps line of the summary and
do not change the status.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, no valid domain, an unreadable input file or an unwritable
output file.
.SH EXAMPLES
All modules except lookalikes, without contacting the target:
.PP
.RS
.B domint example.com
.RE
.PP
Registration and DNS of two domains, then the indicators they share:
.PP
.RS
.B domint \-wd example.com example.org
.RE
.PP
A STIX 2.1 bundle of the lookalike domains, for a threat-intelligence platform:
.PP
.RS
.B domint \-l \-\-stix \-o lookalikes.json example.com
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/rudnikleandro/domint
The project page
.UE
